          "path": "_m/g/c/x/c/hull-minster-wp/glass-mary-hutchinson.jpg",
          "filename": "Hull, Holy Trinity church window (29053166025).jpg",
          "caption": "Glass by Mary Hutchinson, 1920, commemorating the deliverance of Lille and the safe return of Rev. David Keys Moore. Given by James and Catherine Lofthouse, to whom Hutchison was related.\n\nThe design is based on the text \"Therefore, with angels and archangels and with all the company of heaven we laud and magnify thy glorious name\". The four large figures—from left to right—represent Gabriel, Michael, Uriel and Raphael.",
          "alt": "Glass by Mary Hutchinson, 1920, commemorating the deliverance of Lille and the safe return of Rev. David Keys Moore. Given by James and Catherine Lofthouse, to whom Hutchison was related.\n\nThe design is based on the text \"Therefore, with angels and archangels and with all the company of heaven we laud and magnify thy glorious name\". The four large figures—from left to right—represent Gabriel, Michael, Uriel and Raphael.",
          "width": 2587,
          "height": 3833,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 2.0",
          "artist": "Jules &amp; Jenny from Lincoln, UK",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hull,_Holy_Trinity_church_window_(29053166025).jpg",
          "sourceType": "core",
          "sourceArticleId": "hull-minster-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "gcxc"
